  "rendered": {
    "title": "Chat-first onboarding and a hardened hosted harness path",
    "intro": "Today's nightly reshapes Aura's first-run experience around chat, teaches the web and desktop shells to pick the right entry point for their platform, and lands a substantial reliability pass on the hosted local-harness transport — including auth scoping, autospawn safety, and a runtime-capability API so the UI stops offering local agents it can't actually reach.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "11:26 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-03T06:26:50.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-04T15:33:59.000Z",
        "title": "Platform-aware, chat-first onboarding",
        "summary": "Onboarding was rebuilt around the chat surface and now branches by platform, and the desktop shell is correctly classified as a desktop client rather than a native/mobile runtime.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Rebuilt the welcome and onboarding checklist to be chat-first and platform-aware: web users land on the public chat surface, while desktop opens directly into the Build workspace via a new platform entry redirect.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "3dc1cc59c80fa3522fb59dbf0aab6db3c1a2b611",
              "81f739b78bd07907149057eb51a0ebb3aeef7da8",
              "52149ec8fbb47fb6c3ab947faed42a9a9b7bca33"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Renamed the Projects app to Build across the sidebar switch, registry, and search placeholders, and reordered the Build ↔ Agents toggle to match the new default.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "3dc1cc59c80fa3522fb59dbf0aab6db3c1a2b611"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Fixed a desktop misclassification where the loopback origin made isNativeRuntime() return true, which was serving the mobile login view and shell to Desktop; the check now defers to the Tauri/desktop bridge globals so Capacitor and mobile-dev webviews remain native.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "cf021f8018c2b725e20c253e8cf93987c09c53c1",
              "9f38fe85cd0ac79831e136567742a55453502904"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "10:52 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-04T17:52:50.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-04T22:50:35.000Z",
        "title": "Hosted harness transport auth and autospawn safety",
        "summary": "The hosted local-harness path gained a scoped transport bearer, safer autospawn behavior, and matching deployment docs so remote harnesses can be reached without leaking service secrets or accidentally launching a stray local process.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added a dedicated hosted-harness transport auth token that authenticates the server-to-harness hop, and reworked the harness gateway, proxy access layer, and clients to scope it distinctly from the caller's JWT.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5a400c226cc00f75905e23978a099b3bbced42de",
              "8213491cf89acf706935d32e1008d3918c87a59a"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Hardened autospawn so it only fires for real loopback URLs with an explicit port — a hosted LOCAL_HARNESS_URL can no longer silently fall back to 127.0.0.1:8080 and launch an unrelated local harness.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "b4709af0d501d8c029eab6860ecb524ad2826e0c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Documented the hosted-harness deployment story in the README and render-deployment guide, including the LOCAL_HARNESS_AUTH_TOKEN / AURA_NODE_AUTH_TOKEN pairing and the incompatibility with AURA_REMOTE_ONLY=1.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "90b08976e8df8f46324b6beefc407134ce2b5973",
              "b4709af0d501d8c029eab6860ecb524ad2826e0c"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "4:45 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-04T23:45:30.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-04T23:45:30.000Z",
        "title": "Pinned macOS runner for desktop validation",
        "summary": "The desktop validation workflow now runs on a pinned macOS image to stabilize signing and packaging checks against GitHub runner drift.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Pinned the macOS runner used by the desktop-validate workflow to keep desktop bundle validation reproducible across nightly runs.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "e695517ce851e535b57d7259b13044d32019c0c1"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-4",
        "time_label": "5:03 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-05T00:03:25.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-05T00:12:15.000Z",
        "title": "Runtime capabilities API for hosted local agents",
        "summary": "The server now advertises whether a hosted local-harness runtime is actually reachable, and the interface uses that signal instead of assuming based on browser vs. desktop.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added a /api/system/runtime-capabilities endpoint that reports remote_only, hosted_local_harness, and local_agent_runtime_available, gated on a non-loopback LOCAL_HARNESS_URL.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "d0229e6d1fa5cc061fcafcda0ce06a9347db1920"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Wired the new capability into useAuraCapabilities and the agent index/chat routes so cached local-agent ids no longer resolve on clients that can't reach them, and updated the disabled-send copy to say the local agent isn't available in this browser.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "d0229e6d1fa5cc061fcafcda0ce06a9347db1920",
              "558b0c81b3c4a28a091a74d72b14850d47c58b78"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-5",
        "time_label": "6:15 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-05T01:15:29.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-05T01:23:52.000Z",
        "title": "Fail-closed harness auth and public chat import after sign-in",
        "summary": "Hosted-harness auth now fails closed when misconfigured, and signed-in users can promote their guest public-chat transcripts into a real Aura chat session.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Made hosted local-harness routes require and validate the transport bearer, rejecting requests when auth is missing or misconfigured instead of silently falling through.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "801dab211cdf66ed4ddb2e640d922ad46851ddd0",
              "49dc4ec68842b39b5f8ba231d5478587faf94698"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added an authenticated import path that copies a guest's localStorage-only public chat turns into a first-class agent chat session on sign-in, with de-duplication, size limits, and a lazy home-project repair for chat agents lacking a project binding.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "833b6b599ef8dfac3ce46a04a41a5becf4ba7769"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-6",
        "time_label": "10:02 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-05T05:02:16.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-05T05:06:12.000Z",
        "title": "Web chat no longer selects cached local agents",
        "summary": "The chat app now consults runtime capabilities when picking an agent, so remote-only clients stop landing on a cached local agent that can't run there.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Threaded remoteOnly into the chat-app agent resolver and left panel so the web selects a web-safe agent (falling back to the CEO agent) instead of restoring a cached local-agent id it can't use.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "e4d2395c6f5f1a333ea0a09a6cab7574b84d1eba"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Followed up on the desktop loopback detection fix with expanded tests around device-info, host-config, and native-runtime to lock in the desktop-vs-native classification.",
            "commit_shas": [
